# Database Design: Ayush AI Migration

## 1. Overview
We are migrating from file-based storage ([registrations.json](file:///Volumes/z21techssd/AI/ayush-app/data/registrations.json), [treatment_feedback.csv](file:///Volumes/z21techssd/AI/ayush-app/data/treatment_feedback.csv)) to a **PostgreSQL** database.

### Why PostgreSQL?
1.  **Relational Integrity**: Ensures clinical records are strictly linked to patients.
2.  **JSONB Support**: Critical for storing semi-structured AI Treatment Plans ([herbs](file:///Volumes/z21techssd/AI/ayush-app/backend/ayush_ml_pipeline.py#568-599), [yoga](file:///Volumes/z21techssd/AI/ayush-app/backend/ayush_ml_pipeline.py#600-631), [diet](file:///Volumes/z21techssd/AI/ayush-app/backend/ayush_ml_pipeline.py#632-665)) and ML Context (Features) without rigid schema constraints.
3.  **Geospatial (PostGIS)**: Essential for the **Public Health Module** to efficiently query "Cases within X km radius" for outbreak detection.

## 2. Schema Design

### A. Patients Table
Stores core demographic and identity information.

| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| [id](file:///Volumes/z21techssd/AI/ayush-app/src/components/layout/Sidebar.tsx#19-70) | UUID | PK | Unique Patient ID |
| `abha_id` | VARCHAR(20) | UNIQUE | ABHA Health ID |
| `first_name` | VARCHAR(100) | NOT NULL | |
| `last_name` | VARCHAR(100) | | |
| [gender](file:///Volumes/z21techssd/AI/ayush-app/backend/utils/validators.py#32-38) | VARCHAR(10) | | Male/Female/Other |
| `dob` | DATE | | Date of Birth |
| `mobile` | VARCHAR(15) | INDEX | Contact Number |
| `email` | VARCHAR(255) | | |
| `city` | VARCHAR(100) | INDEX | For Analytics |
| `state` | VARCHAR(100) | | |
| `pincode` | VARCHAR(10) | INDEX | Geospatial grouping |
| `created_at` | TIMESTAMPTZ | DEFAULT NOW() | |

### B. Medical Records Table (Visits)
Stores the clinical encounter details. Linked to Patient.

| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| [id](file:///Volumes/z21techssd/AI/ayush-app/src/components/layout/Sidebar.tsx#19-70) | UUID | PK | Unique Visit ID |
| `patient_id` | UUID | FK -> Patients | Link to Patient |
| `symptoms` | TEXT | | Doctor's raw notes or transcribed text |
| [diagnosis](file:///Volumes/z21techssd/AI/ayush-app/backend/services/doctor_agent.py#54-65) | VARCHAR(255) | INDEX | Primary condition (e.g., Dengue) |
| `notes` | TEXT | | Clinical observations |
| `visit_date` | TIMESTAMPTZ | DEFAULT NOW() | |

### C. Treatments Table (AI & Feedback)
Stores the AI-generated advice and the doctor's interaction with it.
Linked to Medical Record (1:1 usually).

| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| [id](file:///Volumes/z21techssd/AI/ayush-app/src/components/layout/Sidebar.tsx#19-70) | UUID | PK | Unique Treatment ID |
| `medical_record_id` | UUID | FK -> MedicalRecords | Context of this treatment |
| `ai_plan` | JSONB | NOT NULL | `{ herbs: [], yoga: [], diet: [] }` |
| `ml_context` | JSONB | NOT NULL | Feature Vector: `{ prakriti: "Vata", severity: 7 }` |
| `doctor_feedback` | JSONB | | `{ rating: "positive", comments: "..." }` |
| `is_retrained` | BOOLEAN | DEFAULT FALSE | Has this been used for model training? |

## 3. Migration Plan

### Step 1: Infrastructure
- Set up local PostgreSQL instance or Docker container.
- Install `sqlalchemy` and `alembic` (for migrations) in backend.

### Step 2: Code Implementation
- Create `backend/database.py` (Connection).
- Create `backend/models_db.py` (SQLAlchemy Models).
- Create `backend/services/db_service.py` to handle CRUD.

### Step 3: Data Migration Script
- Write `scripts/migrate_to_db.py`.
- Read [data/registrations.json](file:///Volumes/z21techssd/AI/ayush-app/data/registrations.json) -> Insert into `patients` and `medical_records`.
- Read [data/treatment_feedback.csv](file:///Volumes/z21techssd/AI/ayush-app/data/treatment_feedback.csv) -> Insert into `treatments` (linking to dummy records if patient not found, or matching by ID).

### Step 4: Cutover
- Update [backend/main.py](file:///Volumes/z21techssd/AI/ayush-app/backend/main.py) to use `db_service` instead of file reads.
- Update [retrain_model.py](file:///Volumes/z21techssd/AI/ayush-app/scripts/retrain_model.py) to fetch from DB (`SELECT * FROM treatments WHERE rating='positive'`).
